                                                              "take":  "The earnings-versus-cash-flow divergence Damodaran documents is the single most important number for equity investors right now. A market priced on earnings that are not converting to free cash flow is a market priced on faith. His 63% shareholder-return ratioÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âthe worst since 2004ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âis a concrete warning sign that AI capex is cannibalizing the actual returns investors own. Until FCF conversion recovers, valuations built on headline EPS deserve a healthy discount, and any portfolio leaning heavily on AI beneficiaries should be stress-tested against his expensive-dead-end scenario, not just the bull case.",
