                                                              "take":  "Santoli is marking an important psychological inflection: the market has moved from \u0027AI will change everything, buy anything adjacent\u0027 to \u0027show me the money,\u0027 and that transition typically compresses multiples across an entire sector before fundamentals catch up. The 20% semiconductor pullback he references is a leading indicator that institutional investors are updating their probability weights on the AI capex cycle extending at the same rate. The actionable implication is to stop treating the semiconductor cohort as a monolith: companies with locked-in hyperscaler contracts and diversified end markets will weather the transition; pure-play AI capex proxies without recurring revenue are now genuinely at risk of missing already-revised-down estimates.",
