                                                                                "summary":  "Damodaran dissects the VC industry\u0027s structural bias toward scaling over profitability, triggered by Vinod Khosla\u0027s tweet that every business should prioritize scaling. He builds a taxonomy of business outcomes showing that most companies chasing the scaling playbook lack the unit economics or competitive moats to make it work. He argues the gray market, the dominance of passive investing, and VC\u0027s power-law return structure all reinforce a system where participants rationally bet on scale regardless of business model quality.",
