                                                                                "take":  "Brown\u0027s bull case is emotionally compelling but analytically thin on the question that matters most: what is the return on this capital? Cloud revenue growth is real, but it is being paid for by the same tech companies building the infrastructure ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â a circular loop that can sustain itself only if downstream AI monetization materializes for enterprise customers. The most important thing to track is not whether compute demand grows (it will) but whether the hyperscalers\u0027 customers are generating enough incremental economic value from AI to justify continued spend. If enterprise AI ROI stalls, the infrastructure bull case collapses faster than Brown acknowledges.",
