                                                                                "summary":  "Brown profiles Ron Baron of Baron Capital, who has managed the top-performing US mutual fund since 2003 and estimates he has returned over $60 billion to investors. Baron\u0027s most consequential call was buying Tesla at a split-adjusted $14/share in 2014 and holding through constant criticism; the firm now holds a $5 billion Tesla position and a $25 billion SpaceX stake. Baron\u0027s philosophy centers on extreme conviction and multi-decade holding periods, with an explicit willingness to ignore media noise and position-size constraints that hamper most institutional managers.",
